Alpha; this is glibc on any platform and the real reason behind
this are ITAR regulations we all love so deeply.

An old Slackware distribution was using libc5, where crypt functions
were not split into a separate library, and yes, C-standard
**requires** for 'main()' to return 'int'.

  Michal


