> news is a 670?
> -ls- 

My Alpha is an AlphaStation 200 4/233 I bought from Onsale.com sometime
around May(?).  The 670 is the vector of the machine checks I've been
having.  I've only seen it recently (last two months or so) about 3 or 4
times.  According to Jay Estabrook, the 670 type are:

 670     Processor Uncorrectable   unrecoverable cache or TLB errors, or
                                   read of a non-existent I/O space
                                   location

I'm hoping this is a software (kernel) problem and not a hardware issue.

