I sent an email to Leonard Zubkoff asking about this on 1/11/99 and
how I could be of help.  He has not replied, and I have not pursued
the matter further.

The latest Buslogic/Mylex Flashpoint driver on 

http://www.dandelion.com/Linux/BusLogic.html

is x86 only.  This is the driver in 2.1.132.  I haven't checked if it
has been changed in 2.2.0pre-*; that seems unlikely...

Enclosed at the bottom is my post to this list of 1/11/99, which I
also sent it to faq-maintainer@redhat.com, hoping that the Alpha
Hardware compatibility list would be revised, but that hasn't
happened.

So, if you are on a non-x86 machine, it doesn't matter if you
configure your kernel with the Flashpoint option
(CONFIG_SCSI_OMIT_FLASHPOINT is not set in your .config); the driver
code is hardwired to silently omit Flashpoint support for you if
__i386__ is not defined...

Cheers,
Craig
