and have encountered a baffling phenomenon (at least for me).  One of our
executables, after being built successfully, refuses to, well, execute:

cetacea (43) ./daaxp_linux
bash: ./daaxp_linux: No such file or directory

cetacea (44) ls -l ./daaxp_linux
-rwxr-xr-x   1 rgd      users     1774918 Jan 29 18:03 ./daaxp_linux

cetacea (45) file ./daaxp_linux
