        libm.so.6.1 => /lib/libm.so.6.1 (0x0000015555f3c000)
        libc.so.6.1 => /lib/libc.so.6.1 (0x000001555606c000)
        libSM.so.6 => /usr/X11R6/lib/libSM.so.6 (0x000001555624e000)
        libICE.so.6 => /usr/X11R6/lib/libICE.so.6 (0x000001555635c000)
        /usr/lib/ld.so => /lib/ld-linux.so.2 (0x0000000000000000)


Note that I use ./ to preface my calls, so there should not be any PATH
concerns here.  Ok, I'll make sure it's in a directory with execute
permissions:

cetacea (49) pwd
/tmp

cetacea (50) ls -ld /tmp
drwxrwxrwt   3 root     root         1024 Jan 30 10:41 /tmp


Other executables that we've built work just fine.

Any clues for somebody who is, apparently, clueless?

Thank you.

